IMPORT prelude
-- EXACTLY in a LATER argument of an action pattern.
--
-- An action is a pattern, and `EXACTLY e` pins an argument to the value of an
-- expression rather than binding a fresh name to whatever turns up. That
-- expression has to be read where the pattern was written.
--
-- It was not. `PatApp0` handed the ambient environment to the FIRST
-- sub-pattern and `PatApp1` then handed each later sub-pattern the environment
-- the PREVIOUS sub-pattern had produced — the bindings it made, not the scope
-- it was written in. So `EXACTLY <a top-level name>` worked in argument one
-- and reported `is not in scope` in argument two:
--
--     PARTY alice MUST Pay (EXACTLY alice) payee              -- worked
--     PARTY alice MUST Pay payer (EXACTLY theLandlord)        -- "not in scope"
--
-- The sibling `FOLLOWED BY` frames (`PatCons0`/`PatCons1`) always carried the
-- ambient environment separately; `PatApp1` now does too. Found while building
-- EVERY evaluation (EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC phase 2), because the fork
-- example the spec itself writes — `Receipt (EXACTLY theLandlord) (EXACTLY t)
-- (EXACTLY amount)` — is exactly this shape. Nothing about it is quantifier-
-- specific: every rule below binds one PARTY.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Landlord HAS name IS A STRING
    Tenant   HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Wave HAS who   IS AN Actor
    Pay  HAS payer IS AN Actor, payee IS AN Actor
    Note HAS who   IS AN Actor, whom IS AN Actor, what IS A STRING

theLandlord MEANS Landlord OF "Ms Ng"
alice       MEANS Tenant OF "Alice"

-- one argument
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`waves` MEANS PARTY alice MUST Wave (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 7

#TRACE `waves` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Wave alice AT 1

-- two arguments, EXACTLY in the first
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`pays someone` MEANS PARTY alice MUST Pay (EXACTLY alice) payee WITHIN 7

#TRACE `pays someone` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Pay alice theLandlord AT 1

-- two arguments, EXACTLY in the SECOND: this is the case that failed
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`pays the landlord` MEANS PARTY alice MUST Pay payer (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 7

#TRACE `pays the landlord` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Pay alice theLandlord AT 1

-- both pinned
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`alice pays the landlord` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Pay (EXACTLY alice) (EXACTLY theLandlord) WITHIN 7

#TRACE `alice pays the landlord` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Pay alice theLandlord AT 1

-- three arguments: the third is reached through two earlier sub-patterns, and
-- a name bound by an earlier argument is still visible to a later EXACTLY.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`notes the landlord` MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Note (EXACTLY alice) (EXACTLY theLandlord) what WITHIN 7

#TRACE `notes the landlord` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Note alice theLandlord "hello" AT 1

-- a pinned argument that does NOT match still refuses, which is the point of
-- pinning it: the landlord is not Alice's payee here.
#TRACE `alice pays the landlord` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Pay alice alice AT 1
